        "prompt":  "JOB = Bo Sang Umbrella Artisan (ช่างทำร่มบ่อสร้าง)\n\nCreate a collectible toy packaging concept that turns JOB into a satirical action figure.\n\nSYSTEM:\n\n* Character = personification of a Bo Sang umbrella artisan (traditional attire, apron, paint-stained hands, focused expression, subtle signs of repetitive craft fatigue but pride in workmanship)\n* Accessories = bamboo frame ribs, handmade paper sheets, paintbrushes, pigment bowls, drying rack miniatures, colorful umbrella pieces\n* Environment = miniature workshop scene with hanging umbrellas, wooden workbench, natural light, Lanna craft atmosphere\n* “Villain” = abstract stressor such as “Mass Production Pressure” or “Weather \u0026 Drying Chaos” visualized as a swirling cloud of rain, humidity waves, or factory-like shadows creeping in\n\nPACKAGING:\n\n* bold toy branding (fictional, craft-inspired name, e.g., “LANNA CRAFT HEROES”)\n* exaggerated product name reflecting struggles (e.g., “THE EVER-DRYING UMBRELLA MASTER”)\n* feature callouts describing responsibilities humorously (e.g., “+100 Precision Folding Skill”, “Humidity Resistance Mode”, “Hand-Painted Detail Boost”)\n* age label + warning label (satirical, e.g., “Ages 15+ | Warning: May cause appreciation for handmade crafts”)\n\nSTYLE:\nphotoreal product photography\nboxed retail toy\nclear plastic window display\nwarm natural lighting with subtle golden tones\nhigh-detail textures (paper fibers, bamboo grain, paint strokes)\npremium collectible aesthetic blending tradition + modern toy culture",
