        "category":  "อาหาร",
        "prompt":  "THEME: Heat Retention \u0026 Ergonomic Grip Flow (การเก็บความร้อนและรูปทรงจับถนัดมือของแก้วกาแฟ)\nFICTIONAL_BRAND_NAME: THERMOFORM\nFICTIONAL_PRODUCT_NAME: FLOWGRIP COFFEE CUP (แก้วกาแฟทรงโค้งรับสรีระและควบคุมอุณหภูมิ)\nFICTIONAL_SHORT_COPY: Hold the warmth. Shape the experience.\nACCENT_COLORS: Matte Charcoal \u0026 Warm Coffee Brown\n\nTASK: Create a professional design concept and advertisement board presented in a single A4 vertical (portrait) composition, fusing a concept board, brand advertisement, and design development materials.\n\n[CORE VARIABLES]\n\n* THEME: {THEME}\n\n[AESTHETIC \u0026 STYLE]\n\n* Style: Minimal, poetic, intellectual composition. Beautifully balanced, generous white space. Pure seamless white background for easy cutouts.\n* Quality: High-resolution, precise, commercial visual quality.\n* Colors: Neutral base color palette (whites, grays), accented by 1–2 colors dynamically derived from the {THEME} (charcoal + warm brown accents).\n* Textures/Light: Precisely depict material textures such as ceramic, matte glaze, subtle steam condensation, and soft light reflections. Emphasize warmth, tactility, and curvature.\n\n[COMPOSITION - TWO-TIER SYSTEM]\n\nTIER 1: PROCESS DIAGRAM (Top Tier, ~40% of canvas)\n\n* Title: “MOTION TO FORM”. Clean, poetic typography at the top center.\n* Content: A professional process diagram visualizing the transformation of the {THEME} from concept to form in exactly 5 distinct stages, presented in a horizontal flow with delicate small arrows connecting them.\n* Stages (Strict Flow):\n    1. Source of Inspiration: Sketches of coffee cup silhouettes, hand grip studies, and heat zones. Label: “SOURCE OF INSPIRATION”.\n    2. Trajectory/Energy: Flow lines showing heat circulation and ergonomic grip paths. Label: “TRAJECTORY \u0026 ENERGY”.\n    3. Abstracted Lines/Structures: Geometric curves defining grip indentations and wall thickness variation. Label: “ABSTRACTED LINES \u0026 STRUCTURES”.\n    4. Three-Dimensional Form: 3D render showing cup curvature, handle integration, and thermal layering. Label: “THREE-DIMENSIONAL FORM”.\n    5. Completed Design: Final product render from multiple angles — top view and perspective — emphasizing form and usability. Label: “COMPLETED DESIGN”.\n* Formatting: Use delicate sketches, clean line diagrams, and refined render previews with center-aligned English labels and generous spacing.\n\nTIER 2: HERO VISUAL \u0026 ADVERTISEMENT (Bottom Tier, ~60% of canvas)\n\n* Content: A massive, dramatic, high-fidelity hero visual of the finalized coffee cup derived from the process above.\n* Object Selection (Resolved): Premium ergonomic coffee cup with integrated thermal design — sculpted grip surface, optimized wall thickness, and refined minimal handle or handle-less form.\n* Visual Direction:\n    * Slight perspective angle emphasizing curvature and depth\n    * Subtle steam rising from the cup\n    * Minimal coffee surface visible for realism\n    * Focus on material, warmth, and form\n* Advertising Elements:\n    * Brand Name: THERMOFORM (clean modern sans-serif)\n    * Product Name: FLOWGRIP COFFEE CUP\n    * Copy: “Hold the warmth. Shape the experience.”\n* FORMATTING: Arrange brand, product, and slogan with refined typography integrated into the lower composition. Maintain hierarchy and avoid clutter.\n\n[STRICT CONSTRAINTS]\n\n* Must be a single vertical A4 image (aspect ratio 3:4).\n* Strong visual continuity between Tier 1 diagram and Tier 2 product.\n* The product must feel real, manufacturable, and structurally logical.\n* Avoid excessive decoration, chaotic layout, or over-saturated visuals.\n* Maintain premium industrial design aesthetic.",
