        "category":  "อาหาร",
        "prompt":  "THEME: Crispy Fried Bananas, Street Food Energy, Golden Crunch Textures, Tropical Market Vibes\nBRAND_NAME: BANANA FRY FEST 2026\nINDUSTRY_SCENARIO: Street Food Festival \u0026 Cultural Market\nPRIMARY_COLORS: Golden Yellow, Deep Banana Brown, Palm Leaf Green\nSECONDARY_COLORS: Coconut White, Warm Orange, Charcoal Black\nSTYLE_DIRECTION: Playful street-food pop, vibrant, slightly retro, fun and appetizing, Thai tropical market aesthetic\nASPECT_RATIO: 16:9\n\nPlease create a high-fidelity “Event Visual Identity Application Board” based on [Theme: {THEME}], [Brand Name / Event Name: {BRAND_NAME}], and [Industry / Scenario: {INDUSTRY_SCENARIO}].\n\nThis is not a single poster, nor a simple logo design, but a comprehensive display of a brand visual system centered around the event theme. The visuals should resemble a professional design agency’s client proposal overview page, showcasing a complete extension of the event from main visuals, logos, IP characters, auxiliary graphics, to offline spatial materials, signage systems, peripheral stickers, and scene installations.\n\n[Overall Positioning]\nDesign the [{BRAND_NAME}] into an event visual system with distinct recognizability, suitable for offline events, festival markets, brand pop-ups, commercial spaces, cultural tourism activities, or urban public events in the [{INDUSTRY_SCENARIO}] context.\nThe overall design should convey a strong sense of branding, festivity, youthfulness, street-food culture, spatial implementation, and visual unity.\n\n[Aspect Ratio and Presentation]\nAspect ratio: [{ASPECT_RATIO}].\nPresent as a single brand visual system proposal board.\nBackground suggestion: Pure white background color for easy cutouts, allowing different material modules to be clearly arranged like a portfolio showcase.\nThe image should display multiple visual application modules of varying sizes and functions, rather than just one main visual.\n\n[Core Visual System]\nEstablish a unified visual language around the [{THEME}], including:\n\n1. Main Logo / Main Title Design\n\n* Design a striking main title for the [{BRAND_NAME}].\n* The font should have a bold, chunky, crispy feel, inspired by fried batter textures, street signage, and Thai market typography.\n* Incorporate visual elements like banana slices, oil splashes, crunchy crumbs, or sizzling effects.\n* May include English subtitles, dates, locations, event slogans, and other auxiliary text.\n* The main logo should be adaptable for extension to various materials like storefronts, posters, stickers, signage boards, etc.\n\n2. Auxiliary Graphics System\n\n* Automatically generate a set of auxiliary graphic symbols based on the [{THEME}].\n* For example: banana shapes, crispy crumbs, oil bubbles, tropical leaves, stripes inspired by street stalls, price tags, hand-drawn icons.\n* All auxiliary graphics must align with the main visual and avoid becoming cluttered decorations.\n\n3. IP Characters / Mascots / Theme Figures\n\n* Design one or more cute, trendy, and shareable IP characters based on the [{THEME}].\n* Characters can be anthropomorphic fried bananas, smiling banana vendors, or playful food mascots holding skewers or baskets.\n* Characters should appear across different materials, such as storefronts, banners, stickers, signage boards, and check-in installations.\n* Character style should match the overall visual, friendly, appetizing, and highly recognizable.\n\n[Material Application Showcase]\nDisplay a complete set of event materials within the same image, including at least multiple modules from the following types:\n\n1. Large-scale main visual logo or entrance installation (e.g., giant fried banana archway)\n2. Event storefront / street food stall / check-in installation\n3. Booth header / pop-up stall / market stall inspired by Thai street vendors\n4. Pathway flags / hanging flags / banners with tropical food patterns\n5. Signage system (Entrance, Food Zone, Market, Rest Area, Parking, Toilet, etc.)\n6. Sticker system / social media stickers / food icons\n7. Floor signage / arrows shaped like banana slices\n8. Scene-based installations (food seating zone, tasting area, photo spot with oversized fried bananas)\n9. Peripheral materials (wristbands, food tickets, takeaway boxes, paper trays, cups, tote bags, badges)\n\nThese materials should not exist in isolation but form a cohesive brand design system, embodying an extension relationship of “same theme, same colors, same graphic language, different application scenarios.”\n\n[Colors and Style]\nPrimary colors: [{PRIMARY_COLORS}].\nSecondary colors: [{SECONDARY_COLORS}].\nOverall style: [{STYLE_DIRECTION}].\n\nColor requirements:\nHigh recognizability, strong contrast, appetizing and warm tones, suitable for food-related environments. Avoid dull or desaturated palettes. Maintain a unified brand identity.\n\n[Composition and Layout]\nUse a “multi-module brand system showcase board” composition approach.\nDo not create a single poster or just one logo.\n\nSuggested layout:\n\n* Top: Main logo + large fried banana entrance installation\n* Left: Flags, banners, and bold graphic patterns\n* Center: Food stalls, booths, signage systems\n* Right: IP characters, stickers, product packaging, installations\n* Bottom: Arrows, icons, functional signage, auxiliary graphics\n\nMaintain clean spacing, hierarchy, and visual rhythm.\nEach module should look like a real, buildable event element.\n\n[Texture and Implementation Feel]\nInclude realistic material textures such as:\n\n* Printed food packaging paper\n* Kraft paper trays\n* Fabric banners\n* Acrylic signage\n* Metal stall frames\n* Sticker cut edges\n* Street-market style booths\n\nThe design should feel both illustrative and physically producible.\n\n[Text Handling]\nInclude minimal but clear text such as:\n\n* [{BRAND_NAME}]\n* Location\n* Date\n* Event slogan (e.g., “Crispy. Sweet. Irresistible.”)\n* Functional signage (Entrance, Food Zone, Market, etc.)\n\nText should integrate naturally into the design.\nIf text rendering is unstable, prioritize layout and visual consistency.\n\n[Final Effect]\nThe final image should resemble a professional agency-level event branding board, featuring:\nstrong identity, cohesive visual system, rich application materials, lively street-food atmosphere, high commercial usability, and scalability for future events.\n\nPlease avoid:\nSingle poster output, isolated logo, inconsistent styles, cluttered visuals, lack of spatial applications, weak branding system, excessive text noise.",
