        "prompt":  "Based on { THAI BETTA FISH / PLAKAD THAI }, create a high-quality vertical “encyclopedia-style educational infographic image.”\n\nThe Master Prompt:\n\n“A comprehensive scientific educational infographic for the Thai Betta Fish (Plakad Thai). The style is a premium vintage natural-history field guide mixed with a Southeast Asian aquatic biology encyclopedia, using a warm cream-colored parchment background with subtle Thai ornamental borders and scientific illustration aesthetics.\n\nThe layout features a large, highly detailed central illustration of a majestic Thai Betta Fish with flowing fins and realistic iridescent coloration. Include multiple anatomical labels pointing to key features such as:\n- ‘Labyrinth Organ’\n- ‘Caudal Fin’\n- ‘Operculum’\n- ‘Iridescent Scale Structure’\n- ‘Aggressive Display Fins’\n- ‘Bubble Nesting Behavior’\n- ‘Pectoral Fin Mobility’\n\nThe central fish should appear elegant, dynamic, and scientifically rendered like a museum-quality specimen illustration.\n\nSurrounding the center are various carefully organized boxed educational sections including:\n\nQUICK PROFILE\n- Scientific Name: Betta splendens\n- Common Name: Thai Betta Fish / Siamese Fighting Fish\n- Native Habitat: Thailand, Cambodia, Laos\n- Average Lifespan\n- Temperament\n- Water Conditions\n- Conservation Status\n\nCLASSIFICATION TREE\nCreate a clean scientific taxonomy diagram showing:\n- Kingdom\n- Phylum\n- Class\n- Order\n- Family\n- Genus\n- Species\n\nKNOWLEDGE SCORE\nUse elegant star-rating infographic systems for:\n- Aggressiveness\n- Beauty\n- Intelligence\n- Adaptability\n- Rarity\n- Ease of Care\n\nLIFE CYCLE DIAGRAMS\nShow detailed illustrated stages:\n- Egg\n- Fry\n- Juvenile\n- Adult Male\n- Adult Female\n- Bubble Nest Reproduction\n\nInclude arrows and educational progression visuals.\n\nSIZE COMPARISON\nShow a realistic comparison between:\n- Thai Betta Fish\n- Human hand\n- Small aquarium\n- Rice paddy ecosystem\n\nDIET SECTION\nInclude miniature scientific illustrations of:\n- mosquito larvae\n- bloodworms\n- daphnia\n- insects\n- micro crustaceans\n\nAdd educational labels and feeding behavior notes.\n\nHABITAT SECTION\nInclude environmental illustrations or photo-style panels showing:\n- Thai rice paddies\n- lotus ponds\n- canals\n- slow-moving freshwater habitats\n- tropical wetlands\n- traditional Thai aquatic landscapes\n\nAdd water-temperature and ecosystem information overlays.\n\nBEHAVIOR SECTION\nIllustrate and explain:\n- territorial behavior\n- fin displays\n- bubble nest building\n- mating rituals\n- aggression signaling\n\nDID YOU KNOW? BANNER\nCreate a decorative educational banner at the bottom with surprising facts such as:\n- Thai Betta Fish are Thailand’s national aquatic animal\n- They can breathe atmospheric oxygen using a labyrinth organ\n- Wild bettas look very different from modern ornamental breeds\n- Selective breeding created hundreds of tail variations\n\nVISUAL STYLE:\n- vintage scientific encyclopedia\n- museum exhibition poster\n- Victorian natural-history illustration\n- premium educational infographic\n- clean taxonomy design\n- highly detailed biological rendering\n- elegant editorial information layout\n- Thai aquatic cultural influence\n\nCOLOR PALETTE:\nUse natural aquatic and Thai-inspired tones:\n- deep indigo blue\n- emerald green\n- crimson red\n- iridescent turquoise\n- parchment cream\n- aged ink brown\n- muted gold accents\n\nTEXTURE \u0026 DESIGN:\n- parchment paper texture\n- ink illustration details\n- scientific diagram linework\n- botanical illustration influence\n- engraved natural-history aesthetics\n- elegant museum-label typography\n\nTYPOGRAPHY:\nUse:\n- vintage scientific serif fonts\n- museum-style labeling\n- engraved educational typography\n- clean infographic hierarchy\n\nMOOD:\neducational,\ncurious,\nscientific,\nelegant,\nmuseum-quality,\npremium natural-history encyclopedia aesthetic.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- ultra-high-resolution vertical infographic poster\n- highly detailed educational composition\n- print-ready museum quality\n- encyclopedia-style scientific layout\n- premium biology educational artwork.”",
