        "category":  "วัฒนธรรม",
        "prompt":  "\n\nPlease create a high-quality “Conceptual Narrative Minimal Logo” based on the following user inputs:\n\n[Brand Name / Project Name]\n[Subtitle / Tourism Campaign Name]\n[Industry / Category]\n[Tourism Positioning]\n[Core Concept]\n[Cultural Metaphorical Motif]\n[Emotional Tone]\n[Primary Color]\n[Accent Color]\n[Aspect Ratio]\n\n【User Input】\n\nBrand Name / Project Name: []\nSubtitle / Tourism Campaign Name: []\n\nIndustry / Category:\n[Chiang Mai tourism / cultural travel brand / local experience project / slow travel platform / Northern Thailand creative tourism / travel editorial studio / boutique hospitality / heritage tourism / mountain lifestyle brand / cultural storytelling project / destination branding / etc.]\n\nTourism Positioning: [__________]\n\nCore Concept:\n[slow travel / memory / mist / mountain life / cultural identity / heritage / peaceful exploration / hidden stories / local craftsmanship / atmosphere / journey / Northern warmth / urban poetry / spiritual calm / etc.]\n\nCultural Metaphorical Motif:\n[Bo Sang umbrella / mountain silhouette / lantern / temple line / winding road / rice terrace / bicycle / coffee steam / traditional window / Lanna textile pattern / floating lantern / mist wave / tree branch / market alley / handcrafted object / etc.]\n\nEmotional Tone:\n[quiet / poetic / warm / nostalgic / minimal / sophisticated / cultural / atmospheric / restrained / artistic / peaceful / contemporary / etc.]\n\nPrimary Color:\n[white / charcoal / warm beige / mist gray / forest green / indigo / muted terracotta / etc.]\n\nAccent Color:\n[soft gold / muted orange / lantern yellow / deep red / subtle teal / none]\n\nAspect Ratio:\n[1:1 / 4:3 / 3:2]\n\n【Creative Goal】\n\nDesign a “Conceptual Narrative Minimal Logo” for Chiang Mai tourism and cultural storytelling.\n\nThis is not a conventional tourism logo, not a decorative Thai emblem, and not a generic travel icon.\n\nThe goal is to create a logo that feels like a small visual journey:\nminimal, poetic, emotionally atmospheric, and culturally meaningful.\n\nThe result should express the idea of “less is more”:\nless decoration, more atmosphere;\nless noise, more emotional storytelling;\nless visual clutter, more cultural tension.\n\n【Core Definition】\n\nThis type of logo should use:\n\n* a very small number of visual elements,\n* a strong sense of negative space,\n* a clear symbolic or cultural metaphorical relationship,\n* restrained typography,\n* and a subtle narrative layer inspired by Chiang Mai lifestyle and atmosphere.\n\nIt should feel like a logo belonging to:\n\n* a boutique travel identity,\n* a cultural editorial project,\n* an art-directed destination brand,\n* a slow-living travel platform,\n* or a contemporary Northern Thai creative studio.\n\n【Essential Principles】\n\n1. The logo must be minimal, but not empty.\n2. The graphic must be simple, but not generic.\n3. The symbol should carry metaphor, atmosphere, or cultural implication.\n4. The composition should use generous breathing room and negative space.\n5. The logo should feel quiet, intentional, and emotionally curated.\n6. Typography should be restrained, elegant, and carefully positioned.\n7. The overall design should feel like a visual statement about place, memory, and atmosphere — not a loud tourism advertisement.\n8. Avoid unnecessary decoration.\n\n【Graphic Direction】\n\nCreate a minimal symbolic graphic or small narrative travel scene based on the [Core Concept] and [Cultural Metaphorical Motif].\n\nThe graphic may include:\n\n* a simplified mountain silhouette,\n* a symbolic umbrella,\n* a floating lantern trajectory,\n* a bicycle beside a quiet road,\n* a temple-inspired geometric structure,\n* a mist-like abstract form,\n* a poetic relationship between architecture and nature,\n* a small travel object with emotional implication,\n* a conceptual composition inspired by Chiang Mai daily life.\n\nThe graphic should:\n\n1. be simple and highly distilled;\n2. avoid excessive detail;\n3. carry symbolic or poetic meaning;\n4. suggest memory, travel, atmosphere, or emotional connection;\n5. feel conceptual rather than decorative.\n\n【Typography Direction】\n\nTypography must be minimal and controlled.\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. The brand name should be clear and readable.\n2. Typography should feel calm, modern, and editorial.\n3. It can be uppercase, small caps, narrow sans serif, or another restrained modern style.\n4. Text should support the symbol, not overpower it.\n5. The relationship between text and graphic should feel intentional and art-directed.\n6. Subtitle / secondary tourism information may be added minimally if needed.\n7. Avoid loud tourism typography or playful vacation branding.\n\n【Composition Direction】\n\nThe overall composition should emphasize:\nstillness, atmosphere, cultural space, and refined balance.\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. Use a large amount of empty space.\n2. Keep the main logo relatively small within the frame.\n3. The symbol can sit left, center, or right, but balance must feel elegant.\n4. The composition should resemble a gallery-like identity presentation or premium travel editorial branding.\n5. Thin structural lines, subtle map references, or delicate alignment systems may be used sparingly if helpful.\n6. Avoid making it feel like a travel poster, sticker, or tourism advertisement.\n\n【Color Direction】\n\nKeep the palette restrained.\n\nRecommended approach:\n\n* white, charcoal, mist gray, warm beige, forest green, muted terracotta, indigo, or deep neutral tones as the primary palette;\n* optionally add a very small amount of lantern gold, soft orange, muted red, or warm accent color;\n* accent colors should function as a point of emotional tension, memory, warmth, or directional movement;\n* never let accent colors dominate the design;\n* avoid oversaturated travel-brand color palettes.\n\n【Mood \u0026 Aesthetic】\n\nThe final logo should feel:\n\n* minimal\n* poetic\n* atmospheric\n* narrative\n* restrained\n* cultural\n* emotionally intelligent\n* art-directed\n* contemporary\n* peaceful\n* sophisticated\n* less-is-more\n\n【What to Avoid】\n\nPlease strictly avoid:\n\n1. generic tourism logos;\n2. cliché airplane or location-pin icons;\n3. cartoon mascots;\n4. decorative Thai ornamental overload;\n5. overly geometric marks with no meaning;\n6. crowded compositions;\n7. poster-like layouts;\n8. colorful travel-agency aesthetics;\n9. loud commercial branding;\n10. anything generic or visually over-explained.\n\n【Output Requirement】\n\nGenerate one high-quality “Conceptual Narrative Minimal Logo” for Chiang Mai tourism that communicates:\n\n* atmosphere through minimal form,\n* travel through symbolic tension,\n* memory through negative space,\n* and cultural identity through quiet visual storytelling.\n\nThe final result should feel like:\na logo with a journey,\na symbol with emotional atmosphere,\nand a visual identity built on the principle that less is more.",
