        "prompt":  "A fun prompt for turning logos into brand worlds (Lanna Sky Lantern Edition).\n\nUse the uploaded business logo as the brand source of truth.\nFirst, analyze it and infer:\n(1) key geometric motifs,\n(2) 3–5 color palette swatches,\n(3) edge/line style (rounded vs sharp),\n(4) 3 brand adjectives, and\n(5) logo usage rules (no warping, clearspace, best placement).\n\nThen generate 4 images in a consistent style:\nlow-poly 3D render + claymorphism + soft occlusion shadows, clean, minimal, warm, culturally refined, Northern Thai (Lanna) identity, Silicon Valley pitch deck quality, solid pastel purple background, aspect ratio 16:9.\n\nThe logo must appear cleanly (as decal/signage/paint), never melted, never stretched, never re-drawn incorrectly. Keep the same brand palette across all 4.\n\n⸻\n\nImage 1 — Hero Isometric / Establishing\n\nA 3D isometric illustration of a floating Lanna lantern crafting village on a small island.\nThe environment features:\n\t•\tTraditional wooden houses and bamboo structures\n\t•\tArtisans crafting โคมลอย (sky lanterns) by hand\n\t•\tHanging lanterns glowing softly in warm light\n\t•\tOrganized crafting zones (frame making, paper covering, drying area)\n\t•\tGentle upward motion of a few lanterns being released into the sky\n\nMood: minimal, premium, serene, culturally rich, softly illuminated like twilight.\n\n⸻\n\nImage 2 — Systems View / Ortho Map\n\nAn orthographic top-down “process map” of the same floating island.\nClearly defined zones using abstract visual cues (no small text):\n\t•\tBamboo frame preparation zone\n\t•\tPaper cutting \u0026 decorating zone\n\t•\tAssembly area\n\t•\tDrying / quality check zone\n\t•\tLaunch platform for lantern release\n\nKeep materials consistent (wood, paper, bamboo, soft clay textures).\nDesign should feel like a clean cultural workflow system, not industrial.\n\n⸻\n\nImage 3 — Macro Detail / Close-Up\n\nClose-up cinematic shot of artisans’ hands assembling a lantern frame:\n\t•\tThin bamboo strips being shaped into a circular structure\n\t•\tSoft paper texture being applied\n\t•\tWarm internal glow suggesting future ignition\n\nBackground: softly blurred floating lanterns rising into the sky.\nApply the logo as a crisp decal on a wooden tool box or work panel.\nShallow depth of field, but maintain clarity and cleanliness.\n\n⸻\n\nImage 4 — Brand Application Mock\n\nA clean in-world mockup showing brand application on:\n\t•\tA lantern release platform signboard (wooden)\n\t•\tA transport crate or delivery cart used for lantern distribution\n\nStyle remains minimal, premium, and consistent with clay/low-poly aesthetic.\nThe logo must be clearly visible, properly spaced, and elegantly integrated into the environment.\n\n⸻\n\nIf you want to push this further, I can extend it into a festival-scale world (ยี่เป็ง), or add storytelling layers for educational use such as integrating cultural meaning, sustainability, or STEM concepts into the visual system.",
