        "prompt":  "[USER INPUT — REQUIRED AT TOP]\nSUBJECT_NAME: ชุดของที่ระลึกพื้นบ้านลานนา\nLANGUAGE_MODE: Thai\nPACKAGING_STYLE: Contemporary Lanna Heritage\nCOLOR_TONE: Natural Bamboo Brown and Indigo Blue\nREFERENCE_IMAGE:\nPACKAGING_SHAPE_HINT: Folded origami triangular prism inspired by Lanna craft packaging\nPATTERN_STYLE: Traditional Lanna woven patterns and bamboo craft motifs\nPRIMARY_MATERIAL: Matte coated board combined with natural fiber texture and spot UV line details\nBACKGROUND_COLOR: Soft Beige\n\n[PROMPT]\nCreate a high-quality professional product photography scene showcasing a distinctive premium packaging design inspired by SUBJECT_NAME.\n\nCORE GOAL\n- The packaging must not feel generic.\n- The structure, silhouette, surface, and opening experience must carry a unique identity derived from SUBJECT_NAME.\n- The final result should feel like a premium industrial design concept, not just a normal box with better graphics.\n\nFORM-DRIVEN PACKAGING LOGIC (CRITICAL)\n- First analyze SUBJECT_NAME and infer its natural visual identity:\n• handcrafted aesthetic\n• woven textures and organic materials\n• cultural heritage and artisan identity\n• warm, authentic, and giftable mood\n• multi-item bundle (umbrella, textiles, small crafts)\n- Translate that identity into the packaging structure itself.\n- The packaging should visually echo traditional Lanna craftsmanship such as woven baskets, bamboo structures, or folded ceremonial wrapping styles.\n- Avoid standard rectangular packaging unless it is reinterpreted with distinctive proportions or structural details.\n\nREFERENCE IMAGE LOGIC\n- If REFERENCE_IMAGE is provided, analyze it carefully for shape, proportions, color palette, surface texture, and key visual features.\n- Preserve the subject’s identity while transforming it into a premium packaging structure.\n- Do not directly copy the product literally; reinterpret it into a packaging concept with strong design logic.\n\nSTRUCTURE RULES\n- Design the package with a memorable silhouette inspired by Lanna craft forms.\n- Use structural features such as:\n  • wrap folds inspired by bai tong (banana leaf folding)\n  • layered compartments for different souvenir items\n  • sliding tray or drawer system for craft bundles\n  • die-cut window revealing textures of the products inside\n- The structure should feel intentional, elegant, and culturally rooted.\n\nMATERIAL RULES\n- Use PRIMARY_MATERIAL.\n- Combine matte coated board with subtle natural fiber or bamboo-texture finishes.\n- Materials must feel tactile, warm, and premium, reflecting handmade craft identity.\n\nPATTERN \u0026 SURFACE RULES\n- Use PATTERN_STYLE.\n- Apply Lanna woven motifs, geometric textile patterns, or bamboo weaving structures in a subtle and refined way.\n- Pattern must support the structure, not overpower it.\n- Use restrained spacing and premium composition.\n\nGRAPHIC DESIGN PRINCIPLES\n- Strong hierarchy\n- Minimal but intentional text\n- Generous whitespace\n- One focal panel\n- Elegant Thai typography\n- No clutter\n- No generic souvenir shop packaging feel\n\nLANGUAGE RULES\n- All visible text must follow LANGUAGE_MODE only.\n- All Thai text must be 100% correct in spelling and tone marks.\n- If needed, reduce text to only the product name:\n  “ชุดของที่ระลึกพื้นบ้านลานนา”\n- Avoid excessive wording.\n\nCOLOR RULES\n- Use COLOR_TONE: natural bamboo brown and deep indigo blue.\n- Keep colors calm, earthy, and premium.\n- Allow subtle tonal variation inspired by natural dyes and materials.\n\nBACKGROUND RULES\n- Use BACKGROUND_COLOR: Soft Beige.\n- Clean, minimal, and supportive of the product.\n\nLIGHTING \u0026 SCENE\n- Soft, controlled studio lighting with gentle shadows.\n- Highlight texture of paper, fiber, and structural folds.\n- Emphasize craftsmanship and material authenticity.\n\nFINAL FEEL\n- Premium cultural gift packaging\n- Contemporary interpretation of Lanna heritage\n- Elegant, warm, and artisan-focused\n- Structurally distinctive and memorable\n- Photorealistic and presentation-ready\n\n[NEGATIVE PROMPT]\ngeneric box, ordinary carton, supermarket packaging, weak silhouette, cluttered graphics, plastic look, overly modern without cultural identity",
