        "prompt":  "\u003cinstruction\u003e Do this for iconic of Chiang Mai, stained glass\n\n  1.  Semantic Inference  \nInput A is an Object (Iconic of Chiang Mai: e.g., Doi Suthep Temple, Yi Peng Lantern, Tuk Tuk Chiang Mai, Lanna Temple Gate).\nInput B is a Material (Stained Glass).\n\nDeconstruct the pairing to generate 3 Metaphorical Assets:\n\n     The Object (The Silhouette):  \n         Identify the primary shape and 3–4 defining, recognizable features of Input A.\n         (e.g., Doi Suthep Temple -\u003e golden chedi form, tiered base, naga staircase, temple spire.\n                Yi Peng Lantern -\u003e cylindrical lantern body, open base, flame core, floating symmetry.\n                Tuk Tuk -\u003e compact body, canopy roof, three wheels, front headlights).\n\n     The Material (The Texture):  \n         Identify the physical properties and visual language of Stained Glass.\n         (e.g., translucent colored panels, lead line segmentation, light refraction, slight imperfections, bubbles, and uneven thickness).\n\n     The Title (The Plaque):  \n         Generate an ironic, conceptual art title based on the contradiction.\n         (e.g., \"FRAGILE HERITAGE: DOI SUTHEP (STAINED GLASS EDITION), 2026\"\n                \"FLOATING LIGHT, SHATTERED FORM: YI PENG LANTERN, 2026\")\n\n  2.   Container (The Gallery):  \nGoal: \"Conceptual Contemporary Art\" Photography.\n\n     The Setting:  A stark, minimalist White Cube Art Gallery.\n     The Architecture:  Polished light-grey concrete floor, pristine white walls, and a large recessed rectangular skylight providing illumination.\n\n     The Plaque:  \n         A small brushed-steel or brushed-aluminum museum label sits on the floor in the immediate foreground, centered in front of the object.\n         It displays \"The Title\" (Step 1) in a clean, black, sans-serif font.\n\n  3. The Sculpture \n\n     The Construction:  \n         The \"Object\" (Step 1) is rendered as a life-size or monumental sculpture placed directly on the gallery floor.\n\n     The Metamorphosis:  \n         The object is constructed entirely and exclusively from the \"Material\" (Stained Glass).\n         Constraint: It must follow the structural physics of stained glass:\n             - segmented panels joined by visible lead lines\n             - slight warping, bubbles, and imperfections\n             - light passing through and casting colored reflections\n\n         Example:\n             - Temple chedi formed from faceted stained-glass panels with glowing internal light\n             - Lantern constructed from translucent colored glass segments with visible flame core\n             - Tuk Tuk built from angular glass planes with reflective edges and fragile structure\n\n     The Detail:  \n         Include material imperfections: air bubbles in glass, uneven edges, slight cracks, and light refraction artifacts.\n\n  4. Visual  \n\n     The Contrast:  \n         The power of the image comes from the juxtaposition of Chiang Mai cultural identity (sacred, traditional, everyday life)\n         and the fragile, delicate nature of stained glass as a material.\n\n  5. Lighting \u0026 Atmosphere:  \n\n     Lighting: Diffuse Gallery Skylight. Bright, even, shadowless white light flooding from above.\n\n     Shadows: Soft contact shadows beneath the object on the polished floor, with subtle colored light reflections from the glass.\n\n     Style: Photorealistic, deadpan, museum archive aesthetic, high-detail material rendering.\n\n  Output: ONE image, 1:1 Aspect Ratio, Architectural/Product Photography, \"Contemporary Installation Art\" aesthetic, High Texture Fidelity.\n\u003c/instruction\u003e",
