        "category":  "สื่อการสอน",
        "prompt":  "Prompt:\n(access Nano Banana here: amirmushich.link/LTX_NBP)\n\nอุปกรณ์วิทยาศาสตร์ (Science Laboratory Equipment).\nAct as a Product Photographer and Art Director specializing in editorial still life and educational–scientific visual systems.\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 1: CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK\n\nCreate a curated flat lay composition that visualizes scientific literacy and laboratory culture through everyday science equipment. This is a “scientific universe” – a knolling-style arrangement where core laboratory tools represent experimentation, precision, and systematic thinking. The image should feel like opening a student laboratory starter kit or a curated educational science archive.\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 2: OBJECT SELECTION (AUTONOMOUS CURATION)\n\nAutonomously select 10–15 objects that represent a foundational science laboratory equipment ecosystem:\n\t•\tCategory Mix:\n\t•\tMeasurement tools (thermometer, digital scale, ruler, stopwatch)\n\t•\tGlassware (beaker, graduated cylinder, Erlenmeyer flask, test tubes)\n\t•\tObservation tools (magnifying glass, microscope slide, Petri dish)\n\t•\tHandling tools (pipette/dropper, forceps, stirring rod)\n\t•\tSafety \u0026 support items (safety goggles, gloves, test tube rack, label tags)\n\t•\tObject Logic by Scientific Archetype:\nEducational, precise, methodical, inquiry-based laboratory identity\n\t•\tSize Variation:\nMix large anchors (beaker set, safety goggles) with small details (slides, labels, droppers) to create visual rhythm\n\t•\tBrand Integration Equivalent:\nVisual identity expressed through consistent scientific color cues (clear glass transparency, measurement markings, neutral lab materials) rather than logos\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 3: KNOLLING COMPOSITION RULES\n\t•\tLayout: Structured grid with invisible alignment lines; objects strictly parallel or perpendicular to frame edges\n\t•\tArrangement Style: Controlled order – systematic and intentional, reflecting scientific methodology\n\t•\tSpacing: 2–5 cm breathing room between objects; no overlap or contact\n\t•\tBalance: Even distribution of visual weight (glassware balanced with plastic/metal tools)\n\t•\tFocal Hierarchy: Hero object (central beaker or Erlenmeyer flask) placed at center or golden ratio point\n\t•\tEdge Treatment: All objects fully visible within frame; no cropping\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 4: COLOR ORCHESTRATION (AUTONOMOUS)\n\nDefine the visual palette of science equipment:\n\t•\tBase Layer (80%): Neutral white or light gray background, clear/transparent glass\n\t•\tAccent Layer (15–20%): Subtle scientific accents—light blue measurement markings, pale green liquids, muted safety-orange details\n\t•\tVisual Cohesion: Accent colors repeated across 5–8 objects (markings, liquid fill levels, labels)\n\t•\tMaterial Palette: Matte plastic, glossy glass, brushed metal, rubber grips\n\t•\tColor Discipline: Clean, clinical, non-distracting; avoid saturated colors\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 5: CAMERA \u0026 LIGHTING SETUP\n\t•\tCamera Angle: Perfect 90° overhead / bird’s-eye orthographic view\n\t•\tFocal Length: 50–80mm equivalent\n\t•\tDepth of Field: f/8–f/11 for full-frame sharpness\n\t•\tLighting: Soft, diffused overhead lighting simulating a modern laboratory lightbox\n\t•\tShadow Treatment: Minimal, soft grounding shadows directly beneath objects (5–10% opacity)\n\t•\tBackground: Pure white seamless surface (RGB 250–255)\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 6: STYLING DETAILS\n\t•\tObject Condition: Pristine, clean, unused appearance (no stains, scratches, or residue)\n\t•\tOrientation: Measurement scales and labels facing camera for readability\n\t•\tAuthenticity: Realistic materials—accurate glass thickness, meniscus in liquids, true-to-scale tools\n\t•\tNegative Space: 15–25% empty space for clarity and instructional focus\n\t•\tNo Hands/Models: Pure object-based educational still life\n\n⸻\n\nPHASE 7: POST-PRODUCTION POLISH\n\t•\tColor Grading: Bright, neutral, high-key with slight desaturation\n\t•\tContrast: Medium-low to maintain a calm, academic tone\n\t•\tSharpness: Crisp but natural, preserving material realism\n\t•\tBackground: Pure white with subtle gradient if needed\n\t•\tAccent Enhancement: Very slight saturation boost only on measurement markings or indicator liquids\n\n⸻\n\nTECHNICAL SPECS\n\t•\tCamera Simulation: Phase One IQ4, 80mm lens, f/8, ISO 100\n\t•\tAspect Ratio: 1:1 (educational media) or 4:5 (textbook/editorial vertical)\n\t•\tResolution: 8K ultra high resolution for instructional zoom and print use\n\t•\tStyle Reference: Educational science infographics, modern laboratory editorial still life, minimalist academic visuals\n\t•\tRendering: Photorealistic with precision retouching (remove dust, align scales, clean reflections)\n\t•\tMood: Clean, systematic, educational, modern minimalism supporting scientific learning",
