        "prompt":  "3D Infographic Diorama Blocks\n(Primary Science — Extended Set, Absolute Non-Repetition Edition)\n\n2x2 Grid , 4 NEW primary-level science topics\n(style: 3D Infographic Diorama Blocks)\n\n\u003cinstructions\u003e\n\nAbsolute Restrictions:\n• Topics must be appropriate for primary school level.\n• Must NOT repeat or overlap with ANY previously mentioned topics including:\n  Water Cycle, Plant Life Cycle, States of Matter, Simple Electric Circuit,\n  Day and Night, Food Chain, Sound Waves, Magnetism,\n  Weather Formation, Human Digestive System,\n  Butterfly Metamorphosis, Push and Pull Forces, Soil Layers,\n  Heat Transfer, Moon Phases, Skeleton \u0026 Muscles,\n  Static Electricity, Seasons, Simple Machines,\n  Animal Adaptations, Light Reflection.\n\n• All 4 chosen topics must belong to DIFFERENT science strands.\n• No conceptual overlap allowed.\n\nAI must select 4 completely different foundational topics such as (examples only, must not reuse earlier themes):\n\nLife Science options:\n• Pollination Process\n• Seed Dispersal Methods\n• Human Respiratory System (basic level)\n• Plant Parts \u0026 Functions\n• Microorganisms (friendly introduction)\n\nPhysical Science options:\n• Gravity in Everyday Life\n• Friction\n• Light Refraction (basic prism example)\n• Density (floating vs sinking)\n• Balanced vs Unbalanced Forces\n\nEarth \u0026 Space options:\n• Rock Cycle (basic level)\n• Earth’s Rotation and Orbit (without repeating Day/Night concept)\n• Types of Clouds\n• Volcano Structure (not tectonics)\n• Fossil Formation\n\nEnergy \u0026 Systems options:\n• Renewable vs Non-Renewable Energy\n• Solar Energy Conversion\n• Water Filtration Process\n• Recycling Process\n• Basic Circuit with Switch (if clearly distinct from earlier electric circuit mention, otherwise choose alternative)\n\nFor each topic:\n\nAnalyze and visually structure:\n• Core concept\n• Step-by-step flow or interaction\n• Clear cause-and-effect relationships\n• Recognizable components\n• Observable results\n\nEach panel must be:\n• A chunky 3D infographic block\n• Toy-like educational diorama\n• Transparent cutaways when helpful\n• Exactly 10 labeled-by-shape components\n  (Short, readable, primary-level vocabulary only)\n\nColor System (AI inferred per panel):\n• [COLOR1] = main system/process flow\n• [COLOR2] = secondary interaction or trigger\n• Soft matte plastic + translucent acrylic materials\n\nLighting:\n• Bright classroom tone\n• Soft shadows\n• High visibility and contrast\n\nStyle:\n• Structured\n• Playful but accurate\n• Data-clear without clutter\n• Consistent visual language across all 4 blocks\n\nComposition:\n• 2x2 balanced grid\n• Equal-sized panels\n• Clean neutral background\n• Clear separation between blocks\n\nOutput:\nONE ultra-high-resolution image\nAll topics must be completely new\nZero repetition across all previous prompts\nPrimary-level scientific clarity required\n\u003c/instructions\u003e",
