        "prompt":  "Create a high-resolution 3D academic infographic poster illustrating an instructional innovation designed to address students’ incorrect sentence construction in Present Simple Tense with Adverbs of Frequency, using structured vocabulary card sequencing and student-generated card creation.\n\nMain Concept:\nIdentifying grammatical errors → structured card arrangement practice → conceptual understanding → student-generated vocabulary cards → real-life language application.\n\nVertical Layout (4 Connected Sections, Top to Bottom):\n\nSection 1: Identifying the Learning Problem\n\nVisualize a classroom board displaying incorrect sample sentences such as:\n\n“She always go to school.”\n\n“He play often football.”\n\nTeacher highlighting:\nVerb agreement errors\nIncorrect adverb placement\n\nBoard labeled:\nLearning Gap: Present Simple + Adverbs of Frequency\n\nOverlay keywords:\nGrammar Accuracy\nSentence Structure\nCommon Errors\nDiagnostic Teaching\n\nProfessional academic tone.\n\nSection 2: Vocabulary Card Sequencing Innovation\n\nShow students using physical vocabulary cards containing:\n\nSubject (She / He / They)\n\nVerb (go / plays / studies)\n\nAdverbs of Frequency (always / usually / often / sometimes / never)\n\nTime expressions\n\nStudents arranging cards into grammatically correct order.\n\nClear visual guide:\nSubject + Adverb of Frequency + Verb (base/s form) + Object\n\nOverlay keywords:\nActive Manipulation\nConceptual Clarity\nGrammar Pattern Recognition\nHands-On Learning\n\nSection 3: Concept Consolidation\n\nVisualize students explaining why a sentence order is correct:\n\nJustifying verb agreement (he/she/it + s)\n\nExplaining adverb placement rules\n\nComparison board:\nIncorrect Structure | Correct Structure\n\nArrow indicating transition from guided practice to independent construction.\n\nOverlay keywords:\nRule Internalization\nMetalinguistic Awareness\nReasoned Explanation\nStructural Understanding\n\nSection 4: Student-Generated Vocabulary Cards\n\nShow students designing their own vocabulary cards:\n\nAdding verbs from daily life (eat, play, watch, study)\n\nCreating new sentence combinations\n\nWriting full sentences related to real-life routines\n\nFinal board titled:\n“Daily Life Sentences Using Present Simple + Adverbs of Frequency”\n\nArrow connecting to lifelong language application.\n\nOverlay keywords:\nConcept Synthesis\nCreative Reinforcement\nTransfer to Real Context\nSustainable Learning\n\nVisual Style Requirements:\n\nClean 3D academic infographic.\n\nIsometric perspective.\n\nClear progression arrows:\nProblem Identification → Card Sequencing → Concept Understanding → Student Creation\n\nModern educational innovation poster aesthetic.\n\nProfessional color palette (navy blue, soft green, warm orange accents).\n\nSoft studio lighting.\n\nHigh resolution.\n\nVertical 4:5 ratio.\n\nSuitable for academic presentation, classroom research report, and instructional innovation showcase.",
