        "prompt":  "Ant=“standard” id=“68241”}\nPlease redesign the traditional Lanna Sky Lantern Festival (Khom Loi / Yi Peng Festival) as a commercially viable, mass-producible, fully 3D-printable premium miniature sculpture, and present it as a professional product design board / industrial design proposal sheet.\n\nOriginal Cultural Reference:\n\n* Subject Name: Lanna Sky Lantern Festival (Yi Peng Festival)\n* Cultural Origin: Northern Thailand (Lanna Kingdom)\n* Cultural Style / Heritage: Traditional Lanna Culture, Festival Art, Ritual Celebration\n* Core Elements:\n    Floating sky lanterns (Khom Loi), Lanna temples, monks, lantern release ceremonies, mountain silhouettes, traditional architecture, decorative tung banners, community gathering, candlelight atmosphere, sacred spiritual symbolism.\n\nDesign Objective:\n\nTransform this iconic cultural festival from an ephemeral event into a collectible three-dimensional miniature sculpture that possesses:\n\n* Collectible Value\n* Display Value\n* Educational Value\n* Cultural Heritage Value\n* Museum Gift Shop Value\n* Commercial Product Value\n\nThe final design must be instantly recognizable as the Yi Peng Lantern Festival while also functioning as an independent work of contemporary sculptural design.\n\nPositioning:\n\nMuseum Cultural Merchandise\nPremium Art Collectible\n3D Printable Display Model\nMiniature Diorama Sculpture\nDesktop Art Object\nCommercially Manufacturable Product\nHigh-End Cultural Souvenir\n\nVisual Presentation:\n\nPresent the project as a professional industrial design proposal board created by a premium design consultancy.\n\nThe layout should resemble a museum-shop product pitch, featuring:\n\n* Hero render\n* Technical views\n* Exploded assembly diagrams\n* Material studies\n* Manufacturing breakdowns\n\nUse isometric view, 45-degree product presentation view, and clean exhibition-style layouts.\n\nMinimal background.\nPremium lighting.\nProfessional product-development presentation quality.\n\nCore Design Requirements:\n\n1. Cultural Scene to 3D Sculpture Translation\n\nPreserve the most recognizable visual identity, cultural atmosphere, ceremonial rhythm, and emotional spirit of the Yi Peng Festival.\n\nTransform:\n\n* Floating lanterns\n* Temple structures\n* Mountains\n* Traditional architecture\n* Monks\n* Festival participants\n* Decorative banners\n* Sacred lantern release rituals\n\ninto physical three-dimensional sculptural components.\n\nDo not create a flat plaque or framed artwork.\n\nInstead, create a fully layered miniature environment featuring:\n\nForeground\nMidground\nBackground\n\nwith strong depth and sculptural presence.\n\nLantern light effects should be translated into layered forms, floating structures, translucent sculptural surfaces, relief patterns, and flowing ornamental geometry.\n\nThe overall composition should immediately evoke the magical atmosphere of thousands of lanterns rising into the night sky above Chiang Mai.\n\n2. Model Structure Design\n\nThe model must function as a complete tabletop collectible sculpture.\n\nThe entire scene should be mounted on a stable artistic base.\n\nPossible base concepts:\n\n* Circular ceremonial platform\n* Temple courtyard base\n* Mountain-inspired terrain base\n* Lantern-shaped pedestal\n* Stylized Lanna cloud platform\n\nThe base should integrate:\n\n* Lanna decorative motifs\n* Traditional Northern Thai patterns\n* Architectural textures\n* Festival-inspired relief carvings\n\nThe structure must have:\n\n* Clear layering\n* Strong depth\n* Stable center of gravity\n* Manufacturing practicality\n\nNo fragile unsupported components.\n\n3. 3D Printing Feasibility\n\nThe design must be suitable for:\n\n* Resin printing\n* FDM printing\n* Modular assembly manufacturing\n\nAll parts should have:\n\n* Adequate thickness\n* Logical support structures\n* Durable connections\n* Production-friendly geometry\n\nThe sculpture should be divisible into modules:\n\n* Base\n* Temple structure\n* Lantern clusters\n* Human figures\n* Decorative elements\n* Support components\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Thin unsupported rods\n* Fragile floating parts\n* Impossible overhangs\n* Deep inaccessible cavities\n* Structures unsuitable for post-processing\n\n4. Artistic \u0026 Aesthetic Requirements\n\nThe sculpture should balance:\n\nTraditional Lanna Heritage\n+\nContemporary Product Design\n\nMaintain a museum-quality aesthetic.\n\nAvoid toy-like appearances.\n\nTranslate cultural emotions into sculptural language:\n\nSpiritual Atmosphere →\nLayered floating lantern formations\n\nSacred Ritual →\nArchitectural symmetry and ceremonial pathways\n\nDreamlike Festival Mood →\nSoft curved surfaces and ascending compositions\n\nCommunity Celebration →\nClusters of figures and lantern releases\n\nMountain Serenity →\nLayered landscape forms\n\nThe overall visual impact should feel elegant, timeless, and culturally significant.\n\n5. Materials \u0026 Surface Treatment\n\nMaterial references:\n\n* Premium resin sculpture\n* Museum-grade painted collectible\n* Ceramic-inspired coating\n* Matte architectural model finish\n* Fine handcrafted miniature detailing\n\nSurface language should include:\n\n* Subtle relief textures\n* Traditional Lanna ornamentation\n* Lantern paper patterns\n* Temple carving motifs\n* Soft layered sculptural contours\n\nPremium appearance only.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Cheap plastic look\n* Glossy toy finish\n* Overly saturated colors\n\n6. Commercialization \u0026 Manufacturing\n\nThe sculpture must be suitable for:\n\n* Museum gift shops\n* Cultural heritage institutions\n* Art galleries\n* Tourism merchandise\n* Educational collections\n* Designer collectible brands\n\nThe design should balance:\n\nArtistic Value\nManufacturing Feasibility\nDisplay Appeal\nMarketability\n\nThe final concept should feel like a product ready for commercial approval and production.\n\nRequired Presentation Board Content:\n\n* Large central 45° hero render\n* Front view\n* Rear view\n* Left side view\n* Right side view\n* Top view\n* Base structure illustration\n* Exploded assembly diagram\n* Modular component breakdown\n* Close-up detail renders\n* Material \u0026 manufacturing specifications\n* Dimension annotations (mm)\n* Professional title layout\n\nSuggested Titles:\n\n“Lanna Sky Lantern Festival 3D Printable Miniature Sculpture”\n\n“Museum-Grade Collectible Inspired by Chiang Mai Yi Peng Festival”\n\n“Commercial Heritage Miniature Design Proposal”\n\nOutput Mood:\n\nMuseum-grade quality,\ncollectible-level craftsmanship,\nstrong spatial depth,\nprofessional industrial design presentation,\nclean layout,\nhigh-end rendering,\nproduction-ready engineering logic,\ncommercial proposal quality,\npremium cultural storytelling.\n\nDo NOT create:\nflat posters,\n2D artwork reproductions,\nphoto collages,\nfragile unsupported structures,\nimpractical printing geometries,\ntoy-like proportions,\nlow-detail models,\nplastic-looking surfaces,\nor designs that fail to capture the spiri",
