        "prompt":  "[USER_INPUT 1]\nCITY_NAME: เชียงใหม่\nCITY_ENGLISH_NAME: CHIANG MAI\nREPRESENTATIVE_DISH: น้ำพริกหนุ่ม ผักต้ม\nBRAND_NAME: City Flavor Archive\nSLOGAN_COPY: รสชาติแห่งขุนเขา วัฒนธรรม และความทรงจำ\nSEAL_TEXT: Chiang Mai Taste\nLANGUAGE_MODE: Thai\n[PROMPT]\nGenerate a high-end poster for the “City Flavor Archive” series, themed “One City, One Dish”.\n[CORE INFO]\nCity: [CITY_NAME]\nRepresentative Dish: [REPRESENTATIVE_DISH]\nBrand Name: [BRAND_NAME]\nMain Title: Hello [CITY_NAME]\nSlogan: [SLOGAN_COPY]\nSeal Text: [SEAL_TEXT]\nEnglish Auxiliary: HELLO [CITY_ENGLISH_NAME] / ONE CITY ONE DISH\n[COMPOSITION]\nCreate a 4:5 vertical poster.\nPlace [REPRESENTATIVE_DISH] in the foreground as the largest visual subject, occupying the lower half of the image.\nThe dish must look realistic, appetizing, bright, clear, and premium.\nThe dish should be more visually dominant than the background.\n[FOOD RENDERING]\nHighlight:\n\nvibrant roasted green chili texture\nsmoky surface details from charcoal roasting\nfreshly boiled local vegetables\nsteamed pumpkin, cabbage, long beans, eggplant, and leafy greens\nauthentic Northern Thai serving tray (ขันโตก)\nsubtle steam rising naturally\nhandcrafted ceramic dipping bowl\nfresh ingredient realism\npremium food-photography quality\nThe food must feel like a high-end dining brand visual, not a menu item photo or cheap promo graphic.\n[BACKGROUND]\nCreate a layered landmark background representing [CITY_NAME].\nUse:\n\none main iconic landmark:\nWat Phra That Doi Suthep temple and golden chedi\nsemi-transparent secondary landmarks:\nTha Phae Gate, traditional Lanna wooden houses, Bo Sang umbrella motifs\ncity skyline silhouettes:\nChiang Mai Old City skyline and mountain ridges\nlocal architectural atmosphere:\nLanna architecture, temple rooflines, carved wooden details, lanterns, and cultural heritage elements\nThe background should feel like an urban vintage archive with depth and cultural identity.\nAdd retro texture only to the background:\n\nold paper texture\naged wall texture\nhalftone dots\ngrainy printing\nmottled patina\nvintage travel-poster feeling\nDo not let the retro texture darken or dirty the food.\n[TEXT SYSTEM]\nUse [LANGUAGE_MODE] for visible text.\nKeep only core text:\n\nHello [CITY_NAME]\n[REPRESENTATIVE_DISH]\n[BRAND_NAME]\n[SLOGAN_COPY]\n[SEAL_TEXT]\nHELLO [CITY_ENGLISH_NAME] / ONE CITY ONE DISH\nDo not add dates or extra small text.\nThe large title should use bright off-white or warm white calligraphy-style lettering with strong contrast against the background.\n[STYLE]\nHigh-end dining brand poster, city flavor visual archive, Northern Thai cultural identity, retro printing, landmark overlays, authentic food photography, fashionable, professional, layered, atmospheric, premium editorial food branding.\nColor direction:\n\nroasted green\nearthy bamboo tones\nwarm ivory\naged gold\nterracotta accents\nsubtle Lanna heritage palette\n[STRICT CONSTRAINTS]\nNO menu layout.\nNO cheap promotional graphic.\nNO cartoon style.\nNO grid layout.\nNO merged multi-image collage.\nNO cluttered small text.\nNO darkened food.\nNO low-quality food rendering.\nNO random landmarks.\nNO incorrect text.\nNO unreadable typography.\nNO modern skyscrapers.\nNO generic Thai imagery unrelated to Chiang Mai.\n[FINAL INTENT]\nCreate a premium “City Flavor Archive” poster for [CITY_NAME] and [REPRESENTATIVE_DISH], combining a highly appetizing hero dish of authentic Northern Thai Nam Prik Noom with boiled vegetables, layered Chiang Mai landmarks, refined retro archive texture, minimal typography, and a fashionable high-end dining brand aesthetic that celebrates the culinary identity and cultural heritage of Chiang Mai.",
