        "category":  "อาชีพ",
        "prompt":  "[USER_INPUT]\nTHEME: กระบวนการนิเทศการศึกษา\nMAIN_TITLE: การนิเทศที่สร้างการเปลี่ยนแปลง\nSUBTITLE: ทุกห้องเรียนคือพื้นที่แห่งการเรียนรู้และพัฒนา\nTIME_OF_DAY: ช่วงเช้า\nCITY_STYLE: ชุมชนเมือง\nLANGUAGE_MODE: ไทย\n[PROMPT]\nCreate a large-scale multi-window narrative cutaway illustration based on [THEME].\n[1. CORE CONCEPT]\nThe image should present a complete educational supervision ecosystem as a cutaway cross-section, revealing many rooms, departments, workspaces, classrooms, and professional learning activities simultaneously.\nThe goal is to create the feeling of:\n“One educational system, countless improvement processes happening at the same time.”\nThe illustration should encourage viewers to explore every section and continuously discover new details related to educational supervision, coaching, mentoring, monitoring, evaluation, and professional development.\n[2. CUTAWAY ARCHITECTURE]\nShow the entire [THEME] as a detailed cutaway structure.\nReveal:\n\nmultiple floors\nclassrooms\nsupervision rooms\nacademic departments\nPLC meeting rooms\ninnovation laboratories\nlearning resource centers\ncorridors\nstaircases\nelevators\nwindows\nobservation rooms\nconference rooms\ndata analysis centers\nteacher workspaces\nschool administration offices\nThe exterior shell should remain visible while exposing the internal world.\nThe architecture should feel believable, rich, and full of educational life.\n[3. MULTI-WINDOW STORYTELLING SYSTEM]\nEach visible room, window, or section should contain a different supervision-related story.\nEvery compartment should feel unique.\nExamples:\n\nclassroom observation\ncoaching conversation\nmentoring session\nlesson study meeting\nPLC discussion\ncurriculum planning\nteacher reflection\naction research presentation\nstudent assessment analysis\ninnovation showcase\ndata dashboard review\neducational technology integration\nlearning walkthrough\ninstructional design workshop\nparent communication planning\nprofessional development seminar\nbest practice sharing\nsupervision feedback conference\ncompetency assessment review\nschool improvement planning\nAvoid repeating the same activity.\nEvery room should contribute a new micro-story to the overall educational supervision narrative.\n[4. ENVIRONMENT \u0026 ATMOSPHERE]\nOutside Environment:\nUse [CITY_STYLE] during [TIME_OF_DAY].\nExamples:\n\ncity streets\nschool buses\ncommunity buildings\ntrees\neducational banners\npedestrians\nurban skyline\nmorning activity\nInside Environment:\nWarm inviting lighting.\nProfessional yet supportive atmosphere.\nVisible collaboration and movement.\nRich educational storytelling.\nCreate a strong contrast between the busy exterior community and the dynamic internal learning-improvement processes.\n[5. CHARACTER SYSTEM]\nPopulate the building with many miniature characters.\nRequirements:\n\nschool administrators\nsupervisors\nacademic teachers\nbeginning teachers\nmentor teachers\nstudents\nparents\neducational personnel\nInclude:\n\nvaried ages\nvaried appearances\nvaried clothing\nvaried responsibilities\nnatural interactions\nNo duplicated poses.\nNo repeated scenes.\nEvery character should feel like part of a living educational ecosystem.\n[6. VISUAL DETAILING]\nInclude:\n\nlesson plans\ndigital dashboards\nassessment reports\nclassroom displays\nteaching materials\nbookshelves\neducational technology devices\nPLC boards\ncompetency frameworks\nsupervision forms\naction research posters\ndata walls\nstudent portfolios\ninnovation exhibits\narchitectural details\nlighting fixtures\nmeaningful educational artifacts\nThe image should reward zooming in.\nEvery section should contain meaningful visual information.\n[7. ART STYLE]\nStyle:\n\nhighly detailed hand-drawn illustration\narchitectural cutaway drawing\nnarrative educational storytelling\nminiature world visualization\ncinematic composition\ndelicate linework\nwarm lighting\nrich environmental details\nmodern educational infographic quality\nBalance:\n\neducational supervision framework\nillustrated storybook\nprofessional learning community\nschool improvement ecosystem\n[8. TYPOGRAPHY]\nUse [LANGUAGE_MODE].\nTitle:\n[MAIN_TITLE]\nSubtitle:\n[SUBTITLE]\nTypography should integrate naturally into the illustration without overpowering the artwork.\n[9. COMPOSITION]\nAspect Ratio:\n4:3\nComposition Goals:\n\ndense but readable\nrich but organized\nmany rooms\nmany supervision stories\nstrong architectural clarity\nclear visual hierarchy\nminimal empty space\nSuggested Floor Narrative Flow:\nFloor 1:\nSchool administration, supervision planning, stakeholder collaboration\nFloor 2:\nClassroom observation, coaching, mentoring, lesson study\nFloor 3:\nPLC activities, innovation development, curriculum design\nFloor 4:\nResearch, assessment analysis, reflective practice, school improvement planning\nRoof Level:\nVision, future learning, educational transformation, innovation showcase\n[10. STRICT CONSTRAINTS]\nNO empty rooms.\nNO repeated supervision activities.\nNO large blank areas.\nNO low-detail sections.\nNO blurry rendering.\nNO horror atmosphere.\nNO distorted architecture.\nNO deformed characters.\nNO photorealistic photography style.\nNO single-scene illustration.\nNO identical windows.\nNO exterior-only view.\nNO missing educational storytelling.\nNO generic office building appearance.\nNO random activities unrelated to educational supervision.\n[FINAL INTENT]\nCreate a highly detailed narrative cutaway illustration of [THEME], showing dozens of simultaneous educational supervision processes within a richly detailed architectural cross-section, where every room, window, floor, and department tells a different story of coaching, mentoring, collaboration, assessment, innovation, and continuous school improvement.",
