        "prompt":  "Ultra-clean top-down (90° flat lay) infographic composition.\n\nA perfectly centered white ceramic plate sits on a seamless light background.\n\nOn the plate: [LANNA NORTHERN THAI DISH FROM CHIANG MAI], shown in a precise cross-section or layered cutaway, revealing internal ingredients, textures, and structure with extreme clarity.\n\nExamples:\n• Khao Soi Chiang Mai\n• Sai Ua (Northern Thai Sausage)\n• Nam Prik Noom Set\n• Gaeng Hang Lay\n• Khanom Jeen Nam Ngiao\n• Miang Kham Lanna\n• Nam Phrik Ong\n• Khao Kan Jin\n• Kaeng Khae\n• Traditional Lanna Food Platter (Khantoke Style)\n\nPRIMARY FOCAL POINT (HERO ELEMENT):\n\nAbove the plate, occupying a large portion of the upper canvas, place an oversized floating infographic bubble displaying the scientifically accurate total calorie count for this exact food item and authentic Chiang Mai serving size.\n\nThe calorie bubble is significantly larger than any other element, instantly readable at thumbnail size.\n\nDesign it with strong visual contrast:\n• Bold sans-serif typography\n• Thick outline or semi-transparent glassmorphism\n• Subtle glow or drop shadow\n• Clean premium UI styling\n\nThis is the first thing the eye sees.\n\nSECONDARY ELEMENTS:\n\nSurrounding the plate, fill the remaining space with a dense, high-information infographic system using realistic, accurate nutritional data for this specific Northern Thai dish:\n\n• Nutritional breakdown charts (protein, carbohydrates, fats in exact grams)\n• Dietary fiber and sodium indicators\n• Vitamin and mineral highlights\n• Ingredient percentage bars and rings\n• Traditional preparation temperatures and cooking times\n• Regional ingredient sourcing icons\n• Chiang Mai geographical origin markers\n• Seasonal ingredient availability indicators\n• Measurement scales\n• Cross-section micro-diagrams\n• Data badges\n• Ingredient provenance maps\n• Traditional Lanna culinary technique indicators\n\nAll numbers must reflect real-world nutritional values for the depicted food.\n\nUse thin vector connectors, dotted lines, arrows, pictograms, and radial charts clearly linking data to specific food components.\n\nInclude authentic Chiang Mai and Lanna ingredients such as:\n\n• Northern curry paste\n• Pickled mustard greens\n• Coconut milk\n• Crispy noodles\n• Egg noodles\n• Pork\n• Chicken\n• Sai Ua spices\n• Lemongrass\n• Galangal\n• Shallots\n• Garlic\n• Dried chili\n• Fermented soybean products\n• Local herbs\n• Sticky rice\n• Fresh vegetables\n\nOptional regional identity elements:\n\n• Subtle Lanna geometric motifs\n• Traditional Northern Thai textile patterns\n• Khantoke-inspired decorative rings\n• Doi Suthep silhouette iconography\n• Chiang Mai cultural markers\n• Elegant Lanna ornamental linework\n\nVisual hierarchy rules:\n\n• Calorie bubble = dominant\n• Plate + food = secondary anchor\n• Surrounding data = tertiary but dense and readable\n\nDesign language:\n\nPremium editorial infographic, Apple UI × National Geographic food science × Michelin culinary visualization × Northern Thailand cultural heritage.\n\nExtremely clean, structured, modern, scientifically accurate.\n\nColor palette:\n\n• Natural food colors\n• Monochrome infographic UI\n• One accent color reserved exclusively for the calorie bubble\n• Subtle Lanna-inspired gold accents\n• Warm Northern Thai earth tones\n\nLighting:\n\n• Soft studio lighting\n• Zero clutter\n• Flat background for maximum contrast\n• Crisp shadows\n• Premium food-photography quality\n\nOutput:\n\n1080×1080\n\nUltra-crisp\n\nSocial-feed optimized\n\nNo watermark\n\nMuseum-quality food science infographic\n\nAuthentic Chiang Mai Lanna cuisine visualization\n\nScientific nutritional accuracy\n\nProfessional editorial design\n\n8K detail\n\nMasterpiece",
