        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT (กรอกแนวคิดโลโก้สั้นๆ พร้อมเลือกสีพื้นหลังและสีตัวโลโก้)\n\nLOGO_CONCEPT_DESCRIPTION: โลโก้ขนมจีนน้ำเงี้ยว\n\nCANVAS_BACKGROUND_COLOR: Bright chartreuse lime-green (#C2F142)\n\nLOGO_SOLID_COLOR: Monochrome black (#000000)\n\nPROMPT LOGIC\n\nCAMERA AND COMPOSITION\n\n* Viewpoint: Sharp, straight-on flat lay orthographic showcase view facing the matrix presentation grid directly.\n* Visual Execution: High-end graphic design presentation layout. Maintain absolute crisp line clarity from edge to edge with zero perspective distortion, zero perspective warping, and zero global blurring.\n* Shot Type: Full-frame avant-garde visual identity matrix presenting 24 vastly distinct, independent, non-repetitive concept explorations simultaneously.\n\nBACKGROUND \u0026 STYLISTIC CANVAS\n\n* Base Backdrop: A solid flat panel coated entirely in CANVAS_BACKGROUND_COLOR filling the frame seamlessly.\n* Layout Architecture: A clean structural matrix consisting of 24 highly individualistic brand logotypes, conceptual marks, and artistic symbols arranged into a tight 6 rows and 4 columns grid.\n* Density: Balanced distribution with even negative space margins, functioning as a high-concept graphic design presentation poster.\n\nHIGH-CREATIVE AUTOMATIC VARIATIONS LOGIC (ANTI-TEMPLATIZATION)\n\n* Core Directive: Do NOT generate generic corporate emblems, clip art, or basic system-font layouts. Every single one of the 24 slots must interpret LOGO_CONCEPT_DESCRIPTION into a highly creative, clever, and unexpected visual solution inspired by the visual identity of Northern Thai “Khanom Jeen Nam Ngiao” — rice noodles, tomato-based broth, pork ribs, dried cotton tree flowers, chili elements, traditional Lanna culinary culture, serving bowls, chopsticks, steam, and local food heritage.\n* Diversified Design Mutation Matrix:\n    * Row 1 (Witty Metaphors): Focus on unexpected visual puns and clever abstract mergers, blending rice noodles, broth bowls, spices, or Northern Thai culinary elements with hidden optical illusions or negative space tricks.\n    * Row 2 (Bold Avant-Garde): Focus on radical, subverted geometry and heavy streetwear-inspired shapes, using asymmetrical line-weights and broken silhouettes derived from noodle strands, steam patterns, bowls, and Lanna motifs.\n    * Row 3 (Deconstructed Wordmarks): Focus on high-concept custom typography where characters are modified, twisted, fluidly warped, or organically combined with visual identifiers associated with Khanom Jeen Nam Ngiao.\n    * Row 4 (Symbolic Icons \u0026 Micro-Details): Focus on brutalist shapes, sharp visual icons, stylized noodle bowls, chili symbols, floral ingredients, and raw graphic tokens flanked by ultra-clean, minimal text subtitles.\n    * Row 5 (Dynamic Line Weight \u0026 Fluidity): Focus on highly artistic, continuous hand-drawn energy inspired by flowing noodle strands, rising steam, and expressive culinary movement, varying from razor-thin lines to ultra-thick ink strokes.\n    * Row 6 (Framed Signage \u0026 Identity Seals): Focus on premium, unconventional boundary framing, using skewed badge outlines, striking slashes, stamped layouts, and contemporary interpretations of traditional Northern Thai food stall signage.\n* Visual Consistency: All 24 logos must be rendered completely flat as high-fidelity solid shapes using exclusively the LOGO_SOLID_COLOR. No gradients, no drop shadows, and no soft bevels. Ensure ultimate edge sharpness and supreme contrast against the canvas background for maximum creative impact.",
