        "prompt":  "An embossed relief-style architectural poster, Chinese seal-press / paper debossing aesthetic (印压凹凸立体画风), panoramic bird\u0027s-eye view of **Wat Chedi Luang, Chiang Mai, Thailand**.\n\n[OVERALL TECHNIQUE]\n\nThe entire image is rendered as if pressed or embossed into thick ivory-white paper or fine architectural plaster. Every surface is sculpted through subtle relief, delicate shadow transitions, and soft highlights rather than flat color or line art. Employ a minimalist engraved-line technique (极简线描手法) to define the ancient brick geometry, weathered stairways, naga balustrades, temple walls, and architectural edges. The background remains a seamless ivory-white (乳白色) field with no visible horizon or sky detail—only an elegant atmospheric gradient fading into silence.\n\n[LANDMARK SUBJECT]\n\nRender a perfectly symmetrical panoramic bird\u0027s-eye view of **Wat Chedi Luang**, the most iconic historic temple within the Old City of Chiang Mai. Depict the monumental ruined Lanna chedi as the dominant architectural centerpiece, surrounded by its authentic temple courtyard, viharns, ceremonial walkways, stone terraces, ancient brick enclosure walls, guardian naga staircases, Bodhi trees, and traditional Lanna temple compounds. The entire sacred complex extends gracefully along a strong central axis, with balanced architectural elements receding into the distance through diminishing perspective. Every architectural component shares the same monochromatic ivory-white embossed material, distinguished only by relief depth, refined shadows, and delicate engraved linework.\n\n[GOLD ACCENT — HERO STRUCTURE]\n\nThe magnificent ancient **Great Chedi of Wat Chedi Luang** occupies the exact visual center of the composition. Render the entire chedi in an elegant matte gold finish (哑金光质感), carefully emphasizing its weathered brick terraces, stepped geometry, elephant sculptures, sacred niches, and distinctive Lanna architectural proportions. Allow a restrained warm white glow (低亮度白光) to softly illuminate its edges, creating the impression of sacred inner radiance emerging from the monument itself while preserving the quiet elegance of the overall composition.\n\n[TYPOGRAPHY]\n\nCentered within the composition, positioned just in front of or slightly above the Great Chedi:\n\n**THAILAND | วัดเจดีย์หลวง**\n\nSet in an elegant refined gold serif typeface with balanced proportions. The typography should span approximately half the image width, becoming an integral architectural element without overwhelming the composition.\n\nAt the bottom of the composition:\n\n- Lower left corner:\n  Today\u0027s date in \"YYYY Mon.DD\" format\n\nBoth rendered in the same muted matte gold tone with restrained editorial elegance.\n\n[COMPOSITION]\n\nWide symmetrical composition viewed from a high elevated aerial perspective, looking directly along the principal ceremonial axis of the temple complex. Approximately 60% of the image consists of luminous ivory negative space surrounding and above the architecture, reinforcing serenity, monumentality, and contemplative stillness. The architectural perspective gradually dissolves toward a soft white vanishing point positioned near the upper center of the composition.\n\n[STYLE REFERENCES]\n\nCombine:\n- Akira Yamaguchi\u0027s meticulous architectural observation\n- Tadao Ando\u0027s minimalist spatial philosophy and disciplined symmetry\n- Zao Wou-Ki\u0027s atmospheric abstraction and spatial depth\n- George Segal\u0027s quiet sculptural relief surfaces\n- Wim Wenders\u0027 contemplative architectural framing\n\nThe embossed surface should appear naturally hand-pressed into fine archival paper, exhibiting flawless craftsmanship, subtle relief transitions, immaculate engraved linework, and absolutely no visual noise or artificial artifacts.\n\n[QUALITY \u0026 MOOD]\n\nUltra-high-resolution 8K rendering with exceptionally rich architectural detail throughout. The overall atmosphere should evoke sacred tranquility, timeless dignity, and quiet radiance (宁静辉光), presenting **Wat Chedi Luang** as a contemporary sculptural reinterpretation where the enduring spirit of the ancient Lanna kingdom meets refined modern editorial art.",
