        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT\n\nArt Style Theme: Neo-Expressionist Tactile Sculptural Poster / Northern Mountain Landscape Reverie\n\nCore Subject \u0026 Scenic Focus: A majestic panoramic landscape of Northern Thailand\u0027s mountain ranges, featuring layered mist-covered peaks, rolling forested ridges, ancient terraced hillsides, and a solitary traditional wooden mountain hut nestled among the highlands. The scene is viewed from a slightly elevated perspective, allowing the mountain layers to recede gracefully into the distance while maintaining a powerful sculptural presence.\n\nTextural Materials \u0026 Layers: Slices of actual dried leaves, weathered tree bark, handmade mulberry paper fibers, fragments of moss, and natural lichen textures embedded into the canvas layers; Thick, sculptural impasto ridges of matte forest-green, earthy umber, mist-gray, and muted blue acrylic paint applied with expressive palette-knife strokes; Coarse hand-spun hemp fibers and fine natural grass strands woven organically across portions of the mountains and valleys.\n\nColor Story \u0026 Accent Pops: A deep monochromatic foundation of forest green, slate gray, earthy brown, and cool mountain blue, punctuated by a bold, hyper-saturated streak of vivid sunrise orange or golden morning light sweeping dramatically across one mountain ridge as the primary visual accent.\n\nComposition \u0026 Directional Lighting: A slightly elevated panoramic viewpoint. Harsh, direct early-morning sunlight enters diagonally from the upper-right, striking selected mountain ridges while casting long, dramatic shadows across valleys, emphasizing the sculptural depth of every physical material layer.\n\n------\n------\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCreate a hyper-tactile, high-art promotional landscape poster based on the Art Style Theme.\n\nApply the exact orientation defined in Composition \u0026 Directional Lighting, utilizing hyper-detailed digital macro rendering with absolute zero photographic lens blur across the entire canvas.\n\nThe entire artwork must be rendered as a three-dimensional mixed-media collage with extreme physical depth. Every element must cast realistic, subtle micro-shadows onto the layers directly beneath it.\n\nSURFACE TEXTURES \u0026 MATERIAL LAYERS\n\n1. IMPASTO \u0026 PAINT DROPS:\nSculpt the mountain formations, forests, mist, and landscape contours using heavy three-dimensional oil paint strokes that physically rise from the surface, revealing expressive palette-knife textures, thick impasto ridges, and visible brush marks.\n\n2. RAW MATERIAL INTERACTION:\nIntegrate the composition with the specified organic materials, allowing dried leaves, bark fragments, mulberry paper fibers, moss textures, hemp threads, and natural grass strands to intersect naturally with the mountain landscape. Torn organic edges, fibrous paper textures, and subtle metallic leaf fragments should interact realistically throughout the composition.\n\n3. COLOR DIMENSION:\nExpress the Color Story \u0026 Accent Pops using raw, unblended oil pigments, matte color fields, reflective metallic highlights, and rich sculptural color transitions while preserving the tactile mixed-media quality.\n\nLAYOUT AND ARCHITECTURE\n\nFrame the composition as a sweeping panoramic Northern Thai mountain landscape.\n\nThe layout must feature organic, fluid geometric slices that cut through portions of the mountains, forests, mist, and sky, revealing richly layered abstract artistic textures rather than conventional landscape rendering.\n\nThe entire composition must remain completely open, with absolutely no outer frames, borders, or visible boundary lines enclosing the artwork.",
