        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT\n\nMain Title Text: DOI SUTHEP\n\nArt Motif Color: Rich Lanna temple gold\n\nBackground Canvas: Solid minimalist clean ivory-white canvas backdrop\n\nBackground Layer Motifs:\nTraditional Lanna flame motifs (ลายกนกล้านนา),\nRadiating sacred halo patterns inspired by Phra That Doi Suthep,\nLayered concentric circular motifs symbolizing Buddhist cosmology\n\nMidground Layer Motifs:\nRolling Northern Thai mountain cloud motifs (ลายเมฆล้านนา),\nTraditional Lanna floral rosettes (ลายดอกล้านนา),\nInterlocking temple lattice ornaments inspired by carved teak architecture\n\nForeground Layer Motifs:\nStylized Bodhi leaf patterns,\nSacred Naga scale motifs,\nTraditional Lanna vine scrolls,\nTiny geometric star-flower ornaments inspired by Northern Thai mural paintings\n\n---\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCreate a flat, vertical rectangular minimalist geometric landscape layout poster based strictly on the parameters provided in USER_INPUT.\n\nApply a straight-on flat graphic view composed entirely of structured vector pattern fills, crisp line weights, and absolute zero depth-of-field blur.\n\nThe entire composition must use completely flat ambient graphic illumination with uniform geometric textures and zero physical cast shadows.\n\nThe layout frames the upper negative space and separates the textured landscape layers crisply using USER_INPUT → Background Canvas.\n\n---\n\nVISUAL LAYOUT STRUCTURE (TWO-PART DIVISION)\n\n### 1. UPPER THIRD (NEGATIVE SPACE \u0026 TYPOGRAPHY)\n\n- Leave the upper third of the canvas completely open as clean negative space using USER_INPUT → Background Canvas.\n- Position USER_INPUT → Main Title Text centered horizontally within this upper third quadrant.\n- Render the text in a thin, elegant modern sans-serif typography using USER_INPUT → Art Motif Color, written in all-caps and stacked vertically.\n\n---\n\n### 2. LOWER TWO-THIRDS (LAYERED PATTERN LANDSCAPE)\n\nSaturate the lower two-thirds of the composition with an elegant abstract interpretation of **Doi Suthep**, depicting layered Northern Thai mountain ridges rising toward the sacred summit.\n\nThe landscape is entirely constructed from flat 2D vector geometry using a monochromatic system based on USER_INPUT → Art Motif Color.\n\nGracefully weave flowing white negative-space bands between the mountain layers to evoke drifting mountain mist, sacred clouds, and the cool atmosphere surrounding Doi Suthep.\n\nArrange the patterned mountain layers from back to front as follows:\n\n**BACKGROUND RIDGES**\n\nFill the distant mountain ranges and the sacred summit silhouette using the pattern structures specified in USER_INPUT → Background Layer Motifs.\n\nSubtly integrate the iconic silhouette of **Wat Phra That Doi Suthep\u0027s golden chedi** into the highest ridge as a simplified geometric landmark without disrupting the minimalist style.\n\n---\n\n**MIDGROUND RIDGES**\n\nFill the central mountain slopes using the pattern structures specified in USER_INPUT → Midground Layer Motifs.\n\nIncorporate abstract geometric interpretations of traditional Lanna temple roofs, carved wooden gables, temple stairways, and forest canopies inspired by the Doi Suthep temple complex.\n\n---\n\n**FOREGROUND RIDGES**\n\nFill the nearest mountain slopes and lower landscape using the pattern structures specified in USER_INPUT → Foreground Layer Motifs.\n\nBlend stylized Bodhi leaves, sacred Naga motifs, native Northern Thai vegetation, and flowing ornamental vines into the foreground while preserving the clean geometric rhythm of the composition.\n\n---\n\nLAYOUT BOUNDARIES\n\nThe entire poster layout must remain completely open with absolutely zero outer borders, generic watermarks, framing boxes, logos, or unnecessary typography.\n\nThe overall artwork should evoke the spiritual serenity, sacred mountain landscape, and timeless Lanna identity of **Doi Suthep, Chiang Mai**, expressed through contemporary minimalist geometric design while preserving strong negative space and refined editorial elegance.",
