        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT\n\nMain Pattern Title: LANNA HERITAGE\n\nColor Data Chart:\nLanna Gold C 18 M 32 Y 82 K 8,\nTeak Brown C 35 M 58 Y 78 K 32,\nIndigo Mor-Hom C 88 M 78 Y 32 K 28,\nTemple Ivory C 4 M 4 Y 12 K 0\n\nBase Pattern Elements:\nInterconnected geometric lattice inspired by traditional Northern Thai carved teak window screens, enclosing stylized eight-petaled Lanna floral rosettes, sacred Bodhi leaves, lotus medallions, and flowing Kanok flame motifs rendered in Temple Ivory over a Lanna Gold pattern field.\n\nPendant Accents:\nElegant hanging Lanna ceremonial ornaments featuring miniature **Tung** (traditional Lanna flags), engraved brass temple bells, geometric teakwood charms, and fine golden tassels suspended vertically beneath each decorative border interval.\n\nDeconstruction Modules:\n\nModule 1:\nAn isolated repeating Lanna floral medallion enclosed within its complete geometric lattice unit.\n\nModule 2:\nTechnical line-art wireframe illustrating the structural construction of the Northern Thai lattice geometry and repeating pattern framework.\n\nModule 3:\nExploded blueprint diagram showing the construction of the ceremonial Lanna pendant assembly, including the teak ornament, brass bell, decorative tassel, and suspension system.\n\n---\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCreate a flat, vertical rectangular technical design specification presentation sheet based strictly on the data provided in USER_INPUT.\n\nApply a straight-on flat orthographic graphic layout view split into a left pattern showcase field and a right technical diagram column.\n\nEnsure zero focus blur, zero perspective depth, and completely flat graphic illumination with absolutely no physical shadows.\n\nThe entire layout sits upon a clean ivory-white canvas overlaid with a subtle pale-gray geometric construction grid composed of overlapping sacred circles inspired by traditional Lanna proportional design.\n\n---\n\nVISUAL LAYOUT STRUCTURE (TWO-COLUMN DIVISION)\n\n### 1. LEFT HALF (MAIN PATTERN DISPLAY)\n\nFill the entire left half of the composition from the top margin to the decorative lower fringe with one continuous repeating **Lanna ornamental textile pattern**.\n\n- Generate the repeating pattern using all structural elements specified in **USER_INPUT → Base Pattern Elements.**\n- The pattern should evoke the elegance of traditional Northern Thai temple textiles, ceremonial banners, carved teak architecture, and woven Lanna fabrics while maintaining a clean contemporary technical presentation.\n- The lower edge of the pattern field terminates in a refined scalloped ornamental border inspired by traditional Lanna decorative edging.\n- Hanging beneath each scalloped interval, render the ceremonial ornaments defined in **USER_INPUT → Pendant Accents**, aligned with perfect rhythmic spacing.\n\n---\n\n### 2. RIGHT HALF (TECHNICAL DIAGRAM COLUMN)\n\n#### UPPER RIGHT\n\nArrange a vertical sequence of isolated technical design studies over the construction grid illustrating the structural anatomy of the pattern.\n\nRender each study according to **USER_INPUT → Deconstruction Modules**, presenting the ornament as a professional museum-quality pattern engineering document.\n\n---\n\n#### UPPER-MID RIGHT\n\nPlace **USER_INPUT → Main Pattern Title**\n\ninside a refined thin rectangular border.\n\nUse elegant vertical typography with clean contemporary proportions suitable for museum archives and textile conservation documentation.\n\n---\n\n#### LOWER RIGHT\n\nRender a vertical column of precise solid circular color swatches.\n\nBeside each swatch, display the exact color specifications listed in **USER_INPUT → Color Data Chart** using a clean monospaced technical sans-serif typeface.\n\nMaintain generous spacing, excellent readability, and balanced visual hierarchy.\n\n---\n\nLAYOUT BOUNDARIES\n\nThe entire layout must remain completely open with absolutely zero outer borders, decorative frames, generic watermarks, unnecessary logos, or unrelated typography.\n\nThe finished artwork should resemble a premium museum textile documentation sheet celebrating the geometry, craftsmanship, symbolism, and timeless visual language of **Northern Thailand\u0027s Lanna artistic heritage**, expressed through contemporary technical graphic design.",
