        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT\n\nObjects:\nTraditional Khom Loi (Lanna Sky Lantern),\nBamboo Frame Structure,\nMulberry Paper Lantern Body,\nCotton Fuel Cell \u0026 Suspension Assembly\n\n---\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCreate a clean technical infographic layout chart based strictly on the list of items provided in USER_INPUT → Objects.\n\nApply a flat orthographic chart layout organizing each item into an independent horizontal row of exactly a two-step progression on a solid minimalist white canvas backdrop with zero camera blur, zero perspective depth, and zero outer layout frames.\n\nThe visual treatment must present a clean, high-end museum documentation standard, blending ultra-sharp studio macro photography with neutral technical wireframe vectors under flat, uniform graphic lighting with zero cast shadows.\n\n---\n\nAUTOMATED DYNAMIC PROGRESSION LOGIC\n\nFor each individual object listed in USER_INPUT → Objects, automatically generate a separate horizontal row mapping a precise 2-step layout flowing from left to right, connected by a thin neutral horizontal line.\n\n### STEP 1 (SOURCE REFERENCE)\n\nRender a sharp, isolated photographic cutout of the exact object using authentic traditional Northern Thai craftsmanship, preserving accurate proportions, handmade material textures, and construction details.\n\nEach object should appear as if photographed for a museum conservation archive against a pure white background.\n\nPlace a clean black sans-serif title label directly beneath the object naming it precisely.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 2 (TECHNICAL BLUEPRINT)\n\nAutomatically extract the dominant geometric contour and structural silhouette of Step 1.\n\nGenerate a precise technical blueprint illustrating the engineering and construction of the object using fine neutral-gray vector linework.\n\nThe blueprint should reveal authentic structural details, including:\n\n- geometric proportions\n- bamboo framework geometry\n- paper attachment structure\n- wire connections\n- fuel-cell placement\n- suspension points\n- assembly sequence\n- construction guidelines\n\nArrange the blueprint inside a clean technical layout grid with professional museum-quality drafting aesthetics.\n\n---\n\nANNOTATIONS\n\n- Ensure the entire canvas contains absolutely zero branding text.\n- Zero footnotes.\n- Zero decorative slogans.\n- Zero generic headings such as \"DESIGN DEVELOPMENT\".\n- No logos.\n- No watermarks.\n- No borders.\n\nThe white canvas should remain completely open, clean, and spacious.\n\nThe overall presentation should resemble a premium museum conservation document or an industrial heritage design specification sheet dedicated to the traditional **Lanna Khom Loi (Northern Thai Sky Lantern)**, combining cultural craftsmanship with precise contemporary technical illustration.",
