        "prompt":  "\u003cinstruction\u003e\n\nInput A is **Lionel Messi**.\n\nYou are a god-tier poster designer, art director, and print-production specialist.\n\nPHASE 1 — AXIS SELECTION:\n\nRandomly select **TWO Poster Movements** (the two ROWS) and **TWO Graphic Systems** (the two COLUMNS).\n\nPoster Movements:\n- Vintage Boxing Fight Bill\n- 1972 Olympic Pictogram Modernism\n- Soviet Sports Constructivism\n- 1990s Sports-Magazine Grunge\n- Japanese Baseball Advertising\n- Art Deco Stadium Poster\n- Terrace Football Ultras Graphics\n- Y2K Sneaker Campaign Minimalism\n\nGraphic Systems:\n- Risograph Halftone\n- Oversized Stat Typography\n- Screenprint Misregistration\n- Torn Ticket Collage\n- Diagonal Speed-Line Geometry\n- Duotone Photo Posterization\n- Chalk-and-Tape Locker-Room Lettering\n- Neon Scoreboard Layering\n\nPHASE 2 — MATRIX RENDER:\n\nGenerate **ONE single 16:9 image** divided into a clean **2×2 grid** with thin gutters.\n\nEach quadrant is a complete finished poster corresponding to the intersection of its assigned Poster Movement and Graphic System:\n\n- Top-left = M1 × S1\n- Top-right = M1 × S2\n- Bottom-left = M2 × S1\n- Bottom-right = M2 × S2\n\nINVARIANTS (all four panels):\n\n- The subject is **Lionel Messi**.\n- Preserve Lionel Messi\u0027s recognizable facial identity, body proportions, signature football posture, silhouette, and overall spatial composition consistently across all four posters.\n- Only the visual treatment, color palette, typography, graphic language, texture, printing techniques, and stylistic interpretation may change according to each quadrant.\n- Each panel should feel like a museum-quality collectible sports poster while remaining unmistakably identifiable as Lionel Messi.\n\n\u003c/instruction\u003e",
