        "prompt":  "USER_INPUT\n\nMain Destination Title: CHIANG MAI\n\nMap Subtitle: THE CULTURAL HEART OF NORTHERN THAILAND\n\nLandmass Specification:\nStylized 3D map cut-out profile of Chiang Mai Province with a rich forest-green top plane and light warm-grey structural depth borders.\n\nMetadata Columns:\nLeft: SUMMARY, Symbol, ELEPHANT.\nRight: HISTORY, LANNA KINGDOM MILESTONES.\n\nHistorical Isometric Icons:\nWat Phra That Doi Suthep with its golden chedi,\nTha Phae Gate with ancient brick walls,\nTraditional Lanna teakwood temple viharn with multi-tiered roofs.\n\nModern Isometric Icons:\nKing Power Mahanakhon-style contemporary business tower adapted to Chiang Mai\u0027s skyline,\nChiang Mai International Airport control tower and terminal,\nModern glass convention center,\nMAYA Lifestyle Shopping Center,\nContemporary university landmark representing Chiang Mai University.\n\nHydrological \u0026 Transit Elements:\nCurving light-blue Ping River,\nRed Chiang Mai Songthaew,\nModern orange commuter railway,\nTraditional tuk-tuk,\nBicycle lane.\n\nFooter Data Diagrams:\nLeft:\nLanna Kings timeline with portrait profile blocks.\n\nCenter:\nGreen landscape ribbon graph with circular data markers and blue statistical bar charts representing tourism, culture, and environment.\n\nRight:\nBlue silhouette mini-map highlighting Chiang Mai\u0027s cultural districts and major attractions.\n\n---\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nCreate a flat, vertical rectangular vibrant travel infographic poster based strictly on the parameters provided in USER_INPUT.\n\nApply a straight-on eye-level flat vector perspective with compressed architectural layering, crisp geometric contours, and rich flat color fills.\n\nThe layout must utilize completely flat graphic illustration lighting with uniform tone values, zero physical cast shadows, and a subtle paper-grain texture overlay with absolute zero depth-of-field blur.\n\n---\n\n## VISUAL LAYOUT STRUCTURE (LAYERED MONTAGE PRESENTATION)\n\n### 1. UPPER SKY FIELD (BACKGROUND LAYER)\n\n- Render a bright Northern Thailand sky with soft blue tones and distant mountain silhouettes across the upper third of the composition.\n- Position **USER_INPUT → Main Destination Title** centered across this upper section using massive bold modern sans-serif typography in solid white, partially masked behind the tallest landmarks.\n- Add subtle drifting clouds and distant mountain ridges inspired by Doi Suthep to establish geographic identity.\n\n---\n\n### 2. MIDDLE \u0026 LOWER SKYLINE MATRIX (MIDGROUND LAYER)\n\nArrange a dense editorial-style montage of Chiang Mai\u0027s most recognizable landmarks with minimal negative space, surrounded by flowering trees and lush tropical greenery.\n\n#### BACKGROUND COLUMNS\n\nRender two dominant vertical landmarks:\n\n- Wat Phra That Doi Suthep rising above the mountain landscape.\n- A modern Chiang Mai skyline featuring Chiang Mai University and contemporary business architecture.\n\n---\n\n#### MIDGROUND AXIS\n\nArrange the following architectural landmarks across the central composition:\n\n- Tha Phae Gate\n- Traditional Lanna temple complex\n- MAYA Lifestyle Shopping Center\n- Chiang Mai International Airport terminal\n- Traditional teakwood architecture\n- Lanna cultural museum\n\n---\n\n#### FOREGROUND TIER\n\nPosition recognizable cultural elements naturally throughout the foreground including:\n\n- Bo Sang umbrella displays\n- Yi Peng sky lanterns\n- Lanna market pavilions\n- Traditional handicraft shops\n- Historic city walls\n- Flower gardens\n\nIntegrate blooming pink Wild Himalayan Cherry blossoms and tropical trees throughout the montage.\n\n---\n\n### 3. WATERFRONT BOUNDARY (FOREGROUND BOTTOM LAYER)\n\nStretch the Ping River horizontally across the lower third of the composition.\n\nInclude:\n\n- Nawarat Bridge\n- Red Songthaews\n- Tuk-tuks\n- Cyclists\n- Pedestrian walkways\n- Riverside cafés\n- Traditional long-tail boat\n- Small riverside parks\n- Local commuters\n\nThese elements frame the lower composition while reinforcing the city\u0027s daily life and transportation identity.\n\n---\n\n## LAYOUT BOUNDARIES\n\nThe entire poster layout must remain completely open with absolutely zero outer borders, framing boxes, decorative frames, watermarks, or non-English typography.\n\nThe finished artwork should resemble a premium contemporary tourism infographic celebrating **Chiang Mai** through a harmonious blend of Lanna heritage, modern urban development, iconic architecture, cultural identity, and natural landscape.",
