        "category":  "วัฒนธรรม",
        "prompt":  "Create a 9:16 editorial typography poster from a single human-centered lifestyle moment inspired by the culture and everyday life of Lanna Chiang Mai.\n\nUse oversized typography as the main composition structure. Let the person, movement, traditional architecture, local streets, mountains, temples, markets, or everyday Lanna scene appear inside the letters, pass through them, or break beyond their edges. The image should feel integrated with the type, not simply placed behind text.\n\nTheme: [custom Lanna title]\nSubject: [Northern Thai / Asian / male / female]\nHuman state: [walking / cycling / daily life / traditional activity / festival movement]\nColor palette: [custom]\nSeries: LANNA FRAGMENTS\nYear: 2026\n\n4 directions:\n\n1. TEMPLE PATH — a local person walking through the historic temple grounds of Chiang Mai with dynamic perspective, one foot close to the camera, breaking through oversized typography. Lanna temple roofs, naga stairways, lanterns, and ancient brick walls become part of the letterforms.\n\n2. OLD CITY TRACE — a single person strolling through Chiang Mai Old City from a low angle, with ancient gates, wooden houses, cafés, bicycles, local markets, and traditional architecture embedded inside large typography.\n\n3. MOUNTAIN MEMORY — a peaceful everyday moment featuring a local person with a bicycle or enjoying a quiet morning surrounded by Doi Suthep scenery, rice fields, mist, rivers, traditional wooden houses, and warm natural light, with lifestyle details woven seamlessly into the letterforms.\n\n4. LANNA RHYTHM — expressive movement inspired by Lanna cultural life, such as carrying a bamboo basket, umbrella making, weaving, traditional dance, or walking during Yi Peng or Songkran festivals, combined with bold typography, mostly monochrome tones with one restrained Lanna-inspired accent color.\n\nKeep the layout minimal: one title, \"LANNA FRAGMENTS,\" one short supporting line, and \"2026.\"\n\nUse realistic photography, authentic Northern Thai people, natural skin and hair, genuine Lanna clothing or contemporary local fashion, subtle paper grain, strong negative space, clean editorial composition, and an elegant magazine-quality aesthetic. Incorporate authentic Chiang Mai identity through traditional architecture, local crafts, temples, mountain landscapes, cultural festivals, and everyday community life. Avoid dense text, barcodes, fake brands, logos, URLs, watermarks, plastic skin, and generic poster templates.",
