        "category":  "เชียงใหม่",
        "prompt":  "FASHION CAPITAL TYPOGRAPHIC POSTER – CHIANG MAI, THAILAND\n\nLuxury editorial travel poster in the style of Chiang Mai\u0027s iconic Lanna heritage, artisan craftsmanship, contemporary design culture, and vintage travel posters. The word \"CHIANG MAI\" in huge bold uppercase serif typography fills the composition.\n\nLETTER MAP (one district, landmark, or cultural fashion element per letter, max 3 motifs each):\nEach letter should represent a unique and recognizable part of Chiang Mai\u0027s identity through its historic temples, Lanna architecture, artisan villages, mountain landscapes, cafés, local markets, traditional crafts, textiles, ceramics, umbrella making, silverware, wood carving, lantern festivals, or everyday northern Thai life. Adapt the motifs naturally while maintaining a refined luxury editorial aesthetic.\n\nSuggested motifs:\n- C — Wat Chedi Luang, ancient brick walls, Lanna lanterns\n- H — Handwoven cotton textiles, local weaving traditions, indigo fabric\n- I — Nimmanhaemin creative district, boutique cafés, contemporary galleries\n- A — Warorot Market (Kad Luang), northern produce, flower vendors\n- N — Doi Suthep mountain, forest scenery, temple staircase\n- G — Jing Jai Market, local artisans, handmade crafts\n- M — Bo Sang Umbrella Village, painted paper umbrellas, handicrafts\n- A — Silver Temple (Wat Sri Suphan), traditional silversmith craftsmanship\n- I — Yi Peng sky lanterns, candlelight, festive atmosphere\n\nSIGNATURE PALETTE:\nUse a color palette inspired by Chiang Mai\u0027s warm terracotta temples, aged teak wood, forest greens, mountain mist, indigo textiles, handcrafted paper, golden temple ornaments, and soft ivory tones while preserving elegant vintage colors and museum-print quality.\n\nCITY FLORA:\nInclude native and culturally significant botanical elements such as Dok Ratchaphruek (Golden Shower Flower), orchids, lotus blossoms, frangipani, bamboo, tropical ferns, and native mountain flora naturally spilling from or intertwining with the typography.\n\nCITY OBJECTS:\nIncorporate authentic Chiang Mai cultural objects including Bo Sang paper umbrellas, handcrafted lanterns (Khom Loy), woven bamboo baskets, celadon ceramics, silverware, coffee drippers, traditional Lanna textiles, tuk-tuks, bicycles, long-tail boats on the Ping River, local fruits, and northern Thai culinary elements.\n\nFASHION FIGURE:\nInclude one elegant adult woman dressed in a sophisticated contemporary fashion style inspired by modern Lanna aesthetics, blending luxury tailoring with traditional northern Thai textiles, handwoven cotton, indigo fabrics, silk accents, handcrafted jewelry, or subtle hill tribe-inspired details. She should interact naturally with the environment and cultural elements without dominating the composition.\n\nBelow typography:\nFeature Chiang Mai\u0027s most recognizable panoramic skyline including Doi Suthep, Wat Phra That Doi Suthep, the Old City walls and moat, historic temple silhouettes, Ping River, traditional teak houses, and mountain landscapes in a subtle panoramic composition.\n\nSUBTITLE:\n\"Where Timeless Lanna Heritage Meets Contemporary Creative Elegance.\"\n\nFooter coordinates:\n18.7883° N, 98.9853° E\n\nUltra detailed editorial vector illustration, clean linework, cream paper, soft vintage colors, collectible museum print, premium luxury travel poster aesthetic, 4:5 vertical.",
